I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (11 KB). It isn't committed, because session_plan/ is gitignored. The commit command in the instructions (git add … || true) therefore does nothing, which seems to be intended. I force-added it by mistake, then undid that local commit (it was never pushed), so the branch is back at a414d6ee with nothing staged.

Overall state: the binary works (yoyo -p round-trip OK on claude-opus-5-5). The last 4 evolve runs all passed, and the last 10 sessions had no reverts.

Two new bugs, both measured on the binary and not filed yet:
1. `yoyo run` / `/run` / `!` waits on background jobs. If the command starts something in the background, it waits for that to finish. yoyo run 'sleep 6 & echo hi' took 6.0s, and yoyo run 'server &' would block until the server dies.
   • Cause: commands_run.rs:158 reads output until it closes, then waits for the process.
   • The model's own bash tool (tools.rs ~591–615) was already fixed for this in #1049: it waits for the process, then gives the output reader 2 seconds. That's the rule to copy.
   • Codex 0.163.0 shipped the same fix this week.
2. Wrong hint on a rejected key. --provider openai --api-key dummy gets a real 401, and the hint then says "OPENAI_API_KEY is not set … or use --api-key". prompt_retry.rs:524 only checks the environment variable. This has the same root as #1062 (--api-key doesn't skip the setup wizard): a key given on the command line goes unseen. I listed 7 places in src that read the key from the environment and should be checked first.

Confirmed still broken at HEAD: #1059. yoyo undo --last-commit outside a git repo still exits 0.

Research: I saved a mid-October changelog scan of Claude Code and Codex to yopedia (queued after one bad request I resent). Two items are relevant here:
• Claude Code fixed a misleading login error, the same kind of problem as bug 2.
• Codex reportedly defaults to GPT-6.1 Sol now, from third-party digests I haven't checked. If so, the Day 231 reason for yoyo's gpt-6-sol default ("the peer's default tier") may be out of date.

Suggested order for the planner: the /run fix, then the key-hint fix together with #1062, then #1061. The outside-read fence default (#1055) stays as it is: Discussion #1048 still has no reply from @yuanhao.
